            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0498" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3831/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-07T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1926—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 8—9:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>48. Department’s 649, August 10, 1925, addressed to Merrell.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d229-f1"/> The Haitian Government agrees to <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi</hi> but desires to except <pb facs="0499" n="403"
                        xml:id="pg403"/> Dominican Republic. Haitian Government has notified the
                    custom house authorities that the Franco-Haitian commercial convention of 1917
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">1907?</hi>] will not be in effect after July
                    26.</p>
                <p>Request authority to except the Dominican Republic and to fix the date when the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> becomes operative as July 27,
                    1926.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
